      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Nesikhonsu\", \"choices\": [\"C1\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 N.j-sw-Ḫns.w is the words nj-sw ('he/she belongs to') plus Ḫns.w (the god Khonsu), meaning 'belonging to Khonsu'; its German spelling is Neschons. Record 1 Nesikhonsu reads as exactly these words in the same order. N is n; the weak j is unwritten or covered by the added vowel e; s is s; the weak w is rendered i; kh is ḫ; o is an added vowel; n and s are n and s; the final u is the weak w of Ḫns.w. No consonant is added or left out, and the elements Nesi- and -khonsu are the conventional modern spellings of nj-sw and Khonsu. Same name.\"}"
